wclip (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add BIND env var to control the listen address. Comma-separated
    values produce multiple listeners sharing one PORT.
  * Default bind changed: with BIND unset, wclip now listens only on
    available loopback addresses (127.0.0.1 and [::1]) instead of all
    interfaces. Set BIND=* (or an explicit list) to expose externally.
    The shipped Docker image pins BIND=* so 'docker run -p ...' keeps
    working without per-deployment overrides.
  * Service is no longer enabled or started automatically on package
    install. After install, run: sudo systemctl enable --now wclip.
    Upgrades preserve whatever state the operator has set.
  * Richer --version output: version, commit, build date, Go version,
    os/arch. A plain 'go build' now uses runtime/debug.ReadBuildInfo()
    to fill in commit and dirty status when ldflags are absent.
  * Versioning is now driven by git tags (vX.Y.Z); the debian/changelog
    top entry must match the tag without the 'v'.
  * Maintainer field corrected (no behavior change).

 -- Oleg Pudeyev <code@olegp.name>  Thu, 14 May 2026 09:55:33 -0400

